{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:\"10.1128/aem.68.5.2113-2119.2002\"","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":1,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"11976079","source":"MED","pmid":"11976079","pmcid":"PMC127539","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC127539"]},"doi":"10.1128/aem.68.5.2113-2119.2002","title":"Effect of polyclonal, monoclonal, and recombinant (single-chain variable fragment) antibodies on in vitro morphology, growth, and metabolism of the phytopathogenic mollicute Spiroplasma citri.","authorString":"Malembic S, Saillard C, Bové JM, Garnier M.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Malembic S","lastName":"Malembic","firstName":"Sylvie","initials":"S","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Laboratoire de Biologie Cellulaire et Moléculaire, UMR Génomique Développement Pouvoir Pathogène, Institut de Biologie Végétale Moléculaire, INRA et Université Victor Ségalen Bordeaux 2, Villenave d'Ornon Cedex, France."}]}},{"fullName":"Saillard C","lastName":"Saillard","firstName":"Colette","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Bové JM","lastName":"Bové","firstName":"Joseph M","initials":"JM"},{"fullName":"Garnier M","lastName":"Garnier","firstName":"Monique","initials":"M"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data","related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"5","volume":"68","journalIssueId":1074328,"dateOfPublication":"2002 May","monthOfPublication":5,"yearOfPublication":2002,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Appl Environ Microbiol","title":"Applied and environmental microbiology","essn":"1098-5336","issn":"0099-2240","isoabbreviation":"Appl Environ Microbiol","nlmid":"7605801"},"printPublicationDate":"2002-05-01"},"pubYear":"2002","pageInfo":"2113-2119","abstractText":"Antibodies are known to affect the morphology, growth, and metabolism of mollicutes and thus may serve as candidate molecules for a plantibody-based control strategy for plant-pathogenic spiroplasmas and phytoplasmas. Recombinant single-chain variable fragment (scFv) antibodies are easy to engineer and express in plants, but their inhibitory effects on mollicutes have never been evaluated and compared with those of polyclonal and monoclonal antibodies. We describe the morphology, growth, and glucose metabolism of Spiroplasma citri in the presence of polyclonal, monoclonal, and recombinant antibodies directed against the immunodominant membrane protein spiralin. We showed that the scFv antibodies had no effect on S. citri glucose metabolism but were as efficient as polyclonal antibodies in inhibiting S. citri growth in liquid medium. Inhibition of motility was also observed.","affiliation":"Laboratoire de Biologie Cellulaire et Moléculaire, UMR Génomique Développement Pouvoir Pathogène, Institut de Biologie Végétale Moléculaire, INRA et Université Victor Ségalen Bordeaux 2, Villenave d'Ornon Cedex, France.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Spiroplasma","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"DE","qualifierName":"drug effects"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GD","qualifierName":"growth & development"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"IM","qualifierName":"immunology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Bacterial Outer Membrane Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"IM","qualifierName":"immunology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Immunoglobulin Fragments","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PD","qualifierName":"pharmacology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Recombinant Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":